  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "add22a74-995c-4532-af7b-8c617b836a42",
    "name": "OAN Dashboards (dev)",
    "description": "Public API of the OAN dashboards on the development environment. Every registry chart is served through one endpoint, `GET /api/charts`, backed by the per-registry dashboard services (farmer, livestock, crop sown) and a 15-minute cache.\n\nThe per-service collections call each service directly and only work against local services; this collection checks the deployed environment.\n\n**Request:** `GET /api/charts?charts=<id>,<id>,...`, with optional filters `region`, `zone`, `woreda`, `kebele` (P-codes such as `ET04`), `recordState` and `farmingType`.\n\n**Response:** `{success, data: {<chartId>: {chartName, success, data: [rows], error, executionTime}}, errors, summary: {total, successful, failed}}`. Row fields are those in the owning service's API reference.\n\n**Freshness:** figures can lag the registry by its reporting-view refresh interval plus up to 15 minutes of cache. An `executionTime` near 0 ms means the chart came from the cache.\n\n**Tests** (collection level): HTTP 200, the envelope, no failed chart, the expected fields per chart, and geography codes at the right level (`region_code` = ET + 2 digits, `zone_code` + 2 more, `woreda_code` + 2 more). The level check fails when most codes are off-level, as when a service maps its levels one step too deep; individual units outside the usual chain, such as special woredas, are only logged to the console.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "57831899",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/49316197-add22a74-995c-4532-af7b-8c617b836a42?source=collection_link"
  },
